=== TFIM.qmd ===
PASS: Q4, Q5, Q6, Q7
FAIL:
- Q1: Intro is a single grammatically awkward sentence (line 13: "This post target to pinned down..."). Does not state the Rydberg mechanism (van der Waals blockade) or why the TFIM matters specifically for analog simulation.
- Q2: No formal "Hamiltonian & Rydberg mapping" section header. The mapping from Rydberg Hamiltonian to spin TFIM (lines 87-91) is given without deriving the key substitution $n_i = (1 - \sigma^z_i)/2$. No parameter regime table mapping Rydberg quantities to TFIM parameters. The claim $h_z = \Delta/2 - \sum_j V_{ij}/4$ makes $h_z$ site-dependent (the sum depends on the local environment), contradicting the uniform-field TFIM written on line 89 — this inconsistency is not addressed.
- Q3: The "Interesting transitions" section (lines 85-102) is only ~17 lines covering just two phenomena (checkerboard, QPT) with no theorem callout boxes. No classical simulation barriers section (partially covered in the "Theoretical complexity" section, but not under the right heading). No phase diagram overview.
- Q8: Intro section is 1 sentence. "Interesting transitions" section is ~17 lines, suspiciously short compared to the 95-line "Theoretical complexity" section and the 83-line "Experiment overview".
- Q9: Line 75: "the ground state is QMA-complete problem" — imprecise. The *ground-state energy decision problem* is QMA-complete, not "the ground state" itself. Line 67: "Actrually" typo.
- Q10: Line 91: $h_z = \Delta/2 - \sum_j V_{ij}/4$ is site-dependent, but the Hamiltonian on line 89 uses a uniform $h_z \sum_i \sigma^z_i$. These are inconsistent unless the system has translational invariance, which is not stated.
- Q11: Line 99: "$\nu \approx 0.629$" is stated without specifying that this is the 3D Ising (i.e., 2D quantum TFIM) critical exponent. The same line says "$\nu = 1$ in 1d" — this is the 1+1D Ising QCP value, but it reads as if referring to classical 1D Ising (which has no finite-T transition). The distinction is not made.
- Q12: The Rydberg→TFIM mapping (lines 87-91) is stated without derivation. The substitution $n_i = (1-\sigma^z_i)/2$ that produces the $J_{ij}\sigma^z_i\sigma^z_j$ and longitudinal field terms is not shown. A reader cannot reconstruct the mapping from what is written.
PRIORITY FIX: Q12 + Q10 — the undocumented Rydberg→TFIM mapping with the inconsistent site-dependent $h_z$ undermines the page's central purpose.

