   - **Step 2:** One-dimer-per-vertex constraint → fixed $A_v$ → toric code vertex operator
   - **Step 3:** Closed loop of 6 Rabi flips around a kagome hexagonal plaquette (3 dimers on alternating edges → 5 intermediate constraint-violating states → complementary configuration); amplitude $\sim \Omega^6/\Delta^5$; lower-order processes vanish. This is the $B_p$ plaquette operator.

A reader can now reconstruct the full blockade → toric code mapping without consulting the original paper.

