## Cross-file notation consistency check (Q10)

- **$n_i$**: index.qmd (line 30) defines $n_i = |r_i\rangle\langle r_i|$ as "Rydberg projector (occupation number at site $i$)." All sub-pages use $n_i$ consistently as Rydberg projector. In ferm_Hubbard.qmd, $n_i$ is used for electron number ($n_i = \sum_\sigma c_{i\sigma}^\dagger c_{i\sigma}$) — this is a different model context (not Rydberg), so it is acceptable as a context-dependent notation, though a reader scanning across files could be confused. In Boson-Hubbard.qmd, $\hat{n}_i$ is used for boson number — distinguished by the hat. **Marginal pass.**

- **$\sigma^x_i$ vs $S^x_i$**: index.qmd @eq-tfim uses $\sigma^x_i$ (Pauli operator). The XY/XXZ sections of index.qmd use $S_i^+$, $S_i^-$ (spin-1/2 operators). XY_XXZ.qmd follows this convention. TFIM.qmd @thm-tfim-otoc uses $\sigma^x_i, \sigma^z_i$ (Pauli). **Consistent — the two conventions are never mixed within the same Hamiltonian.**

- **$J$ notation**: In TFIM.qmd, $J$ is Ising coupling ($J = V_{ij}/4$). In ferm_Hubbard.qmd, $J = 4t^2/U$ is superexchange. In XY_XXZ.qmd, $J_{ij} = C_3/R_{ij}^3$ is dipolar exchange. These are different models, so reuse is acceptable. **Pass.**

