## === TFIM.qmd ===
PASS: Q1, Q3, Q5, Q6, Q7, Q8, Q9, Q11, Q12
FAIL:
- **Q2**: No explicit parameter regime table mapping Rydberg quantities ($C_6$, $n$, $a$, $\Omega$, $\Delta$) to TFIM model parameters ($J$, $h_x$, $h_z$). The "convention dictionary" (line 104–125) shows the symbolic transformation but lacks numerical ranges (typical $C_6$ values, $\Omega/2\pi$ in MHz, spacing in μm, etc.) that an experimentalist would need.
- **Q4**: PASS — 16 experiments listed with full detail and summary table. Excellent coverage.
- **Q10**: Line 23 uses `$-J \sum \sigma^z_i \sigma^z_{i+1} - h \sum \sigma^x_i$` (ferromagnetic convention); line 51 of index.qmd uses $\frac{\Omega}{2}\sum_i \sigma^x_i - \Delta\sum_i n_i + \sum_{i<j}\frac{C_6}{R_{ij}^6}n_in_j$ (Rydberg projector convention). The "convention dictionary" box (line 104–125) explicitly reconciles these, so this is handled. However, line 100 writes the Pauli-form Hamiltonian as `$H_{\text{Ryd}} = \sum_{i<j} J_{ij} \sigma^z_i \sigma^z_j - h_x \sum_i \sigma^x_i - h_z \sum_i \sigma^z_i$` **without stating the positive-$J_{ij}$ (AFM) sign convention** before the dictionary box, which appears 4 lines later. A reader encountering line 100 first might assume the condensed-matter convention where $-J$ means FM. Minor but noted.

PRIORITY FIX: Q2 — missing numerical parameter regime table. The page has everything else at a very high standard.

