## Global Cross-File Issues

**Q10 cross-file notation:**
- `$\Delta$` means laser detuning in index.qmd, TFIM.qmd, density_wave.qmd, topological.qmd, LGT.qmd; means vortex gap in honeycomb.qmd (explicitly flagged); means anisotropy in XY_XXZ.qmd (as $\Delta_{\text{anis}}$, subscripted). The honeycomb.qmd is the only page that explicitly flags the overloading. XY_XXZ.qmd relies on the subscript to distinguish but does not call attention to it.
- `$n_i$` consistently means $|r_i\rangle\langle r_i|$ (Rydberg projector) across index.qmd, TFIM.qmd, density_wave.qmd, topological.qmd, LGT.qmd, optimization.qmd. In Boson-Hubbard.qmd, $\hat{n}_i = \hat{n}_{i\uparrow} + \hat{n}_{i\downarrow}$ (total boson number) — different symbol ($\hat{n}$ vs $n$), so no conflict. In ferm_Hubbard.qmd, $n^f_i$ and $n^d_i$ are pseudo-fermion and physical fermion numbers — properly superscripted.
- `$\sigma^x_i$` means Pauli-$x$ on the Rydberg $|g\rangle,|r\rangle$ qubit everywhere except honeycomb.qmd where it labels bond-type coupling (flagged explicitly).

**Q6 cross-file citations:**
- All citation keys verified against refs.bib. No unresolved keys found. No `<!-- TODO -->` markers anywhere.

